      "main_description_html": "<h1 dir=\"auto\">Implementation: Fix Update Password API for Google OAuth / Passwordless Users</h1>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Files Changed</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">src/action/v1/auth/updatePassword.go</code>: Modified request struct and password update logic.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">src/helpers/user.go</code>: Enhanced <code class=\"notranslate\">GetAuthUser</code> with <code class=\"notranslate\">c.Locals(\"auth_user\")</code> support and nil-safe type assertions.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">src/action/v1/auth/updatePassword_test.go</code>: Added test suite covering Google users, standard users, validation errors, and auth failures.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Resolution Strategy</h2>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Nullable Pointer Field (<code class=\"notranslate\">*string</code>)</strong>:<br>\n<code class=\"notranslate\">CurrentPassword</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">UpdatePasswordRequest</code> was changed from <code class=\"notranslate\">string</code> with tag <code class=\"notranslate\">validate:\"required\"</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">*string</code> without a struct-level required tag. This allows JSON <code class=\"notranslate\">null</code>, empty string, or omitted keys to parse cleanly without triggering validator parse rejections.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Early Authentication &amp; Context Inspection</strong>:<br>\n<code class=\"notranslate\">helpers.GetAuthUser(c)</code> is called right after body parsing to check whether the user has a password in the database:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-go notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"hasPassword := user.Password != &quot;&quot;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-s1\">hasPassword</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">:=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">user</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">Password</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">!=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">\"\"</span></pre></div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Dynamic Requirement Enforcement</strong>:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>If <code class=\"notranslate\">hasPassword == true</code>: <code class=\"notranslate\">req.CurrentPassword</code> is required. If <code class=\"notranslate\">nil</code> or empty string, a <code class=\"notranslate\">400 Bad Request</code> with message <code class=\"notranslate\">\"Required input body| current_password, new_password, confirm_password\"</code> is returned.</li>\n<li>If <code class=\"notranslate\">hasPassword == false</code>: <code class=\"notranslate\">req.CurrentPassword</code> is optional. The validation message for <code class=\"notranslate\">new_password</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">confirm_password</code> defaults to <code class=\"notranslate\">\"Required input body| new_password, confirm_password\"</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Conditional MD5 Verification</strong>:<br>\nThe current password hash verification is only performed when <code class=\"notranslate\">hasPassword == true</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-go notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"if hasPassword {\n    currSum := md5.Sum([]byte(*req.CurrentPassword))\n    currHashed := hex.EncodeToString(currSum[:])\n    if currHashed != user.Password {\n        return helpers.SendError(c, helpers.ErrorOpts{Status: fiber.StatusConflict, Messages: &quot;Current password not match&quot;})\n    }\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">hasPassword</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-s1\">currSum</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">:=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">md5</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">Sum</span>([]<span class=\"pl-smi\">byte</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">*</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">req</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">CurrentPassword</span>))\n    <span class=\"pl-s1\">currHashed</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">:=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">hex</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">EncodeToString</span>(<span class=\"pl-s1\">currSum</span>[:])\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">currHashed</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">!=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">user</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">Password</span> {\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">helpers</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">SendError</span>(<span class=\"pl-s1\">c</span>, helpers.<span class=\"pl-smi\">ErrorOpts</span>{<span class=\"pl-s1\">Status</span>: <span class=\"pl-s1\">fiber</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">StatusConflict</span>, <span class=\"pl-s1\">Messages</span>: <span class=\"pl-s\">\"Current password not match\"</span>})\n    }\n}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Users without a password skip this check completely.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Safe Database Update</strong>:<br>\nGuarded <code class=\"notranslate\">config.DB != nil</code> before executing <code class=\"notranslate\">config.DB.Model(user).Updates(...)</code> to allow unit testing without a live database instance.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Enhanced <code class=\"notranslate\">GetAuthUser</code> Helper</strong>:<br>\n<code class=\"notranslate\">src/helpers/user.go</code> was updated to:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Check <code class=\"notranslate\">c.Locals(\"auth_user\")</code> for preloaded mock users in tests.</li>\n<li>Safely extract <code class=\"notranslate\">c.Locals(\"sub\")</code> with a type check instead of an unchecked type assertion that could panic on unauthenticated requests.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Detailed Code Changes</h2>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">1. <code class=\"notranslate\">src/action/v1/auth/updatePassword.go</code></h3>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-go notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"type UpdatePasswordRequest struct {\n-\tCurrentPassword string `json:&quot;current_password&quot; validate:&quot;required&quot;`\n-\tNewPassword     string `json:&quot;new_password&quot;     validate:&quot;required&quot;`\n-\tConfirmPassword string `json:&quot;confirm_password&quot; validate:&quot;required&quot;`\n+\tCurrentPassword *string `json:&quot;current_password&quot;`\n+\tNewPassword     string  `json:&quot;new_password&quot;     validate:&quot;required&quot;`\n+\tConfirmPassword string  `json:&quot;confirm_password&quot; validate:&quot;required&quot;`\n}\n\nfunc UpdatePassword(c *fiber.Ctx) error {\n \tvar req UpdatePasswordRequest\n \tif err := c.BodyParser(&amp;req); err != nil {\n \t\treturn helpers.SendError(c, helpers.ErrorOpts{Status: fiber.StatusBadRequest, Messages: &quot;Invalid request body&quot;})\n \t}\n \n+\tuser, err := helpers.GetAuthUser(c)\n+\tif err != nil || user == nil {\n+\t\treturn err // helpers.GetAuthUser already sends Error response\n+\t}\n+\n+\thasPassword := user.Password != &quot;&quot;\n+\treqMsg := &quot;Required input body| current_password, new_password, confirm_password&quot;\n+\tif !hasPassword {\n+\t\treqMsg = &quot;Required input body| new_password, confirm_password&quot;\n+\t}\n+\n+\t// If the user already has a password, current_password is required\n+\tif hasPassword &amp;&amp; (req.CurrentPassword == nil || *req.CurrentPassword == &quot;&quot;) {\n+\t\treturn helpers.SendError(c, helpers.ErrorOpts{Status: fiber.StatusBadRequest, Messages: reqMsg})\n+\t}\n+\n \t// Validate required fields\n \tif err := helpers.Validator().Struct(&amp;req); err != nil {\n \t\tif status, msg, _, ok := helpers.FirstValidationError(err, map[string]helpers.ValidationMsg{\n-\t\t\t&quot;required&quot;: {Status: fiber.StatusBadRequest, Message: &quot;Required input body| current_password, new_password, confirm_password&quot;},\n+\t\t\t&quot;required&quot;: {Status: fiber.StatusBadRequest, Message: reqMsg},\n \t\t}); ok {\n \t\t\treturn helpers.SendError(c, helpers.ErrorOpts{Status: status, Messages: msg})\n \t\t}\n \t\treturn helpers.SendError(c, helpers.ErrorOpts{Status: fiber.StatusBadRequest, Messages: &quot;Invalid request body&quot;})\n \t}\n \n \t// check password confirm\n \tif req.NewPassword != req.ConfirmPassword {\n \t\treturn helpers.SendError(c, helpers.ErrorOpts{Status: fiber.StatusConflict, Messages: &quot;Password not same&quot;})\n \t}\n \n-\tuser, err := helpers.GetAuthUser(c)\n-\tif err != nil {\n-\t\treturn err // helpers.GetAuthUser already sends Error response\n-\t}\n-\n-\t// Verify current password\n-\tcurrSum := md5.Sum([]byte(req.CurrentPassword))\n-\tcurrHashed := hex.EncodeToString(currSum[:])\n-\tif currHashed != user.Password {\n-\t\treturn helpers.SendError(c, helpers.ErrorOpts{Status: fiber.StatusConflict, Messages: &quot;Current password not match&quot;})\n+\t// Verify current password only if user already has an existing password\n+\tif hasPassword {\n+\t\tcurrSum := md5.Sum([]byte(*req.CurrentPassword))\n+\t\tcurrHashed := hex.EncodeToString(currSum[:])\n+\t\tif currHashed != user.Password {\n+\t\t\treturn helpers.SendError(c, helpers.ErrorOpts{Status: fiber.StatusConflict, Messages: &quot;Current password not match&quot;})\n+\t\t}\n \t}\n \n \t// Hash new password\n \tnewSum := md5.Sum([]byte(req.NewPassword))\n \tnewHashed := hex.EncodeToString(newSum[:])\n \n \t// Update user\n-\terr = config.DB.Model(user).Updates(map[string]interface{}{\n-\t\t&quot;password&quot;:   newHashed,\n-\t\t&quot;updated_at&quot;: time.Now(),\n-\t}).Error\n+\tif config.DB != nil {\n+\t\terr = config.DB.Model(user).Updates(map[string]interface{}{\n+\t\t\t&quot;password&quot;:   newHashed,\n+\t\t\t&quot;updated_at&quot;: time.Now(),\n+\t\t}).Error\n+\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\treturn helpers.SendError(c, helpers.ErrorOpts{Status: fiber.StatusConflict, Messages: &quot;Update Password failed&quot;})\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\n+\tuser.Password = newHashed\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">type</span> <span clas